<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Ceval says in talks to sell soymeal to U.S..</title>
<headline>Brazil Ceval says in talks to sell soymeal to U.S..</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian food processor Ceval Alimentos said it was negotiating to sell 40,000 tonnes soymeal for shipment to the United States in June.</p>
<p>&quot;We are negotiating the sale of some soymeal but we haven't closed anything yet,&quot; said Charles Van Der Heyde, director of external sales.</p>
<p>He provided no further details on the potential sale, including who the buyer might be.</p>
<p>Ceval has its own warehouses at the southern port of Sao Francisco do Sul and is building a terminal there to store soybeans and soyproducts, meaning it can ship product rapidly if necessary.</p>
<p>CBOT soybeans tumbled earlier after Cargill Inc confirmed it was importing Brazilian soybeans for use in processing plants in the southeastern U.S..</p>
<p>((--Joelle Diderich, Sao Paulo newsroom +55 11 248 5417)</p>
